lden  lord but does want us to try it's all  about the struggle it's all about the  suffering and the failing that feeds the  urgery and thus the greater will america  shattered the elden ring in defiance of  the greater will ratagon tried to repair  it because he is still loyal to the  greater will this is why america wants  no one to become elden lord by keeping  the ring shattered she keeps the greater  will weakened hence all the dead fingers  at the divine towers as for gideon he  remarked that a man cannot kill a god  upon his defeat this is referring to the  greater will not america or ratagon he  believes that the player must eventually  be stopped to prevent the elden ring  from being repaired and finally the  greater will itself attacks you in the  form of its avatar the elden beast for  the sole reason of getting a hold of the  runes you have collected and repaired  for it it doesn't want you to become  elden lord as you wouldn't be a puppet  lord like ratagon was you would have  your own free will so it tries to kill  you in order to get the runes and then  find another that can replace ratagon  this is why when you kill the elden  beasts you have effectively killed the  greater will which is why it says god  slain upon its defeat finally depending  on the ending that you choose you can  mend the elden ring yourself you can  give it to ronnie or just destroy  everything with the three fingers in the  flame of frenzy becoming the lord of  chaos so just know when you're out there  playing the game and dying over and over  again to some boss that you're  struggling with you are inevitably  feeding the erd tree and in my opinion  that should piss you off more to  eventually get to the ending where you  can break this cycle and be rid of the  earth tree or you can choose to keep it  going the ending is completely up to you  that's why i love these games man  they're freaking awesome and i have to  preface this in every video all of this  is speculation we are